1
00:00:00,550 --> 00:00:04,038
This company makes over
one million dollars a year.

2
00:00:04,217 --> 00:00:06,989
On paper, business is good.

3
00:00:07,183 --> 00:00:11,238
Annual revenue? S$1.2 million.

4
00:00:11,317 --> 00:00:16,118
Reported profit? S$180,000.

5
00:00:17,217 --> 00:00:20,607
But tonight, the founder
checks the bank account.

6
00:00:21,217 --> 00:00:23,637
S$14,000.

7
00:00:23,850 --> 00:00:27,988
Tomorrow's payroll? S$36,000.

8
00:00:30,017 --> 00:00:31,291
What happened?

9
00:00:31,350 --> 00:00:34,674
Customers pay 90 days after invoicing.

10
00:00:34,783 --> 00:00:36,796
Suppliers want payment now.

11
00:00:37,287 --> 00:00:39,414
And salaries don't wait.

12
00:00:39,983 --> 00:00:42,234
Every new order looks like growth.

13
00:00:42,417 --> 00:00:43,923
But every order also needs

14
00:00:43,923 --> 00:00:46,390
cash before the customer pays.

15
00:00:46,883 --> 00:00:49,951
The company isn't
necessarily losing money.

16
00:00:50,117 --> 00:00:52,904
Its cash is trapped in unpaid invoices,

17
00:00:52,904 --> 00:00:55,152
while real bills keep arriving.

18
00:00:56,717 --> 00:00:59,822
The solution starts with
forecasting cash weekly,

19
00:00:59,822 --> 00:01:01,961
collecting receivables earlier,

20
00:01:01,961 --> 00:01:04,358
negotiating better payment terms,

21
00:01:04,358 --> 00:01:06,568
and maintaining a cash buffer.

22
00:01:07,617 --> 00:01:10,236
Because revenue makes headlines.

23
00:01:10,236 --> 00:01:12,422
Profit looks good on paper.

24
00:01:12,422 --> 00:01:14,844
But cash pays salaries.

25
00:01:15,317 --> 00:01:18,813
A profitable business can
still run out of cash.

26
00:01:19,350 --> 00:01:22,715
Is your business ready for
a 90-day payment delay?

27
00:01:23,083 --> 00:01:26,249
DM me to book a free
cash-flow health check.
